One of my biggest complaint about nethack is that it is almost 
impossiable to figure out what you need to do to finish the game without 
getting outside help.  You have to polypile if you don't get an item that 
you need.  The first time you get to the level of the Medeusa, your going 
to die because you don't know about it, the second time your going to die 
if you think that a sheild of relection will protect you.

One thing that frustrated me about the latest version of nethack was the 
first quest.  I had no clue what I was suppose to do.  I had a hard time 
finding the teleport trap to take me there, mainly because I didn't know 
I was suppose to find one.  I also had a hard time figuring out what I 
was suppose to do when I was in the Quest.  When I had done what I was 
told to do, I had a hard time getting out of the quest, because I had no 
idea where the teleport trap was to get out of it.

I was hoping that oricle would help me by telling me things I should know 
about the game.  Instead I was told a bunch of stuff that I already knew 
having played earlier versions of the game.  There is lots of useful 
information that the oricle could tell me, like things about the Element 
planes or beyond.  I have never been beyond the wand of wishing castle 
and the mazes and I doubt I ever will be.  I get bored with all the 
pointless searching.  As far as I am concerned, the game is only 
interesting at low levels.  After that, it no  longer is a struggle to 
stay alive where knowledge and skill help out.  It becomes a game where 
endless patience and luck are far more important.  All my high level 
charactors get killed by boredom.

